index 0000000..6223745
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fs/filesystems/procfs/docs/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# procfs — Design
+
+## Purpose and scope
+
+`procfs` exposes process, thread, device, and kernel-state snapshots through a
+read-only virtual filesystem. Per-task files are created from published
+`kprocess` identities and weak task references; procfs does not own process or
+MM state.
+
+## Architecture
+
+```text
+published Process / Thread
+          │ resolve a live task
+          ▼
+     procfs task node ─── TaskStat / Process facade
+          │                    │
+          └── format bytes ◄── MM snapshot under LiveAddressSpace
+```
+
+`task_nodes/root.rs` owns `/proc/<pid>` and `/proc/<pid>/task/<tid>` entries.
+The `status` file reports the target task's state and group thread count, then
+formats current `VmSize`/`VmRSS` when the target has a live mm. `statm` formats
+the seven Linux page-count fields from `TaskStat`: size, resident, shared, text,
+zero library, data, and zero dirty-text. A target without an mm yields seven
+zeroes.
+
+`maps` and status/statm use separate snapshots. The numeric memory snapshot is
+copied while a `LiveAddressSpace` capability and MM lock are held; procfs
+formats the returned values after the snapshot. It never reads mapped user
+page contents to report these counters.
+
+## Execution context and lifecycle
+
+Node lookup/read runs in ordinary filesystem task context and may acquire
+sleepable process/MM locks. A node closure stores a `WeakKtaskRef`; each read
+upgrades it and returns `ESRCH` when the task has exited and been reclaimed.
+Directory lookup follows existing `ENOENT` behavior for an unavailable target.
+
+## Compatibility decisions
+
+- `statm` uses base pages; status memory sizes use KiB.
+- `State` describes the selected task. `Threads` is the current process group
+  count.
+- RSS is the MM snapshot's anon/file/shmem category total. Shared is file plus
+  shmem resident pages; physical page mapcount is not used as the definition.
+- The current status implementation intentionally adds the selected
+  `State`/`Threads`/`VmSize`/`VmRSS` subset; full Linux status expansion remains
+  separate.
+
+## Concurrency and failure behavior
+
+The weak task upgrade protects against stale identity access. Procfs does not
+hold process membership locks while acquiring the MM lock. Snapshot failures
+propagate through existing VFS errors; no mapping read or backend I/O is started
+by a status/statm read.
