+
+## Sparse present-leaf range traversal
+
+`PageTable64::visit_present_in_range()` is a read-only observer for rare
+address-space accounting and diagnostics. It descends only through present
+table entries, visits only leaves intersecting the supplied interval, and
+reports a huge leaf once with its base address and page size. Consumers convert huge
+leaves to base-page counts as needed. The visitor does not allocate, mutate
+PTEs, flush TLBs, interpret user/device policy, or read mapped page contents.
+The owner must keep the page table stable for the whole traversal.
